      "title": "IBM and Rutgers control 100 qubits in real time",
      "summary": "Researchers from Rutgers, IBM and partners showed a quantum computer can check what is happening inside it while running and respond, repeatedly resetting parts of the system to tame chaotic behavior. This matters because larger, more reliable quantum machines will need this kind of live feedback. It is still a research demonstration, and useful large-scale machines remain a long way off.",
